{
  "id": "T-1425",
  "created_at": 1790809552.918019,
  "parent": "T-1403",
  "role": "review",
  "tier": "sonnet",
  "complexity": 7,
  "title": "review: fix round 1 for T-1407: treat PermissionError from os.killpg like ProcessLookupError (security review T-1415; folds T-1414)",
  "spec": "Fix round for T-1407, requested by security review T-1415 (request_changes): with the wall-clock deadline loop, os.killpg(proc.pid, 0) in gate._run raises PermissionError (EPERM) on macOS when the group holds only zombies; the reviewer reproduced it in tests/test_gate_timeout.py test_daemon_gate_timeout_holds_as_infra_failure at gate.py:77. This fix round carries the whole T-1414 spec, which is superseded because it depended on T-1407 merging.\n\nWhy: on macOS, os.killpg(pgid, sig) raises PermissionError (EPERM), not ProcessLookupError, when every process left in the group is a zombie. orchestrator/gate.py _run catches only ProcessLookupError around each killpg (lines ~51, 58, 65-66, 71). On 2026-10-01 T-1408's gate went red on tests/test_gate_timeout.py test_cleanup_command_runs_on_timeout with PermissionError at gate.py:65 (the os.killpg(proc.pid, 0) probe after the SIGTERM grace). In production the same race crashes run_gate on a timeout instead of returning timed_out, which the daemon would record as a gate failure.\n\nWhat: in gate._run treat PermissionError exactly like ProcessLookupError at every os.killpg call (the group is gone or unkillable zombies; reap with proc.wait/communicate as today). Keep the return shape and the wall-clock deadline logic from T-1407. Add the test with os.killpg patched to raise PermissionError on the probe and on SIGKILL: run_bounded on a sleeping child with a tiny timeout returns timed_out True and does not raise.\n\nWork in wt/T-1407 on task/T-1407, on top of its commits. Commit first, then run the focused test in the foreground; never background a command, never the full gate.\n\nAlso run tests/test_gate_timeout.py as a whole three times in a row in the foreground before finishing.",
  "inputs": [
    "T-1420"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_gate_timeout.py::test_killpg_permission_error_is_treated_as_gone passes: with os.killpg raising PermissionError for the probe and SIGKILL, run_bounded on a timed-out child returns timed_out True without raising",
    "tests/test_gate_timeout.py::test_deadline_counts_wall_clock_sleep still passes, and tests/test_gate_timeout.py passes three runs in a row",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh wt/T-1407 exits 0"
  ],
  "scope": [
    "orchestrator/gate.py",
    "tests/test_gate_timeout.py"
  ],
  "depends_on": [],
  "constraints": {
    "read_only": true,
    "budget_turns": 20,
    "timeout_s": 900
  },
  "status": "done",
  "assigned_to": "claude:A",
  "worktree": "/Users/k3ntaw/code/orchestrator/wt/T-1425",
  "codex_thread": null,
  "result": {
    "summary": "Implementation matches spec: all four os.killpg call sites in gate._run now catch (ProcessLookupError, PermissionError) instead of ProcessLookupError alone, and the wall-clock deadline loop from T-1407 is preserved with correct return shape. Verified by reading orchestrator/gate.py and tests/test_gate_timeout.py at the T-1407 worktree HEAD (commit 98dfec7), and by running `uv run --project . python -m unittest discover -q tests -p test_gate_timeout.py` three times in a row: 14/14 tests pass each run, including test_killpg_permission_error_is_treated_as_gone and test_deadline_counts_wall_clock_sleep. Traced both subTest iterations (denied_signal=0 and denied_signal=SIGKILL) by hand against the implementation and confirmed each raises PermissionError at the intended callsite and is swallowed, with the process actually reaped via the real SIGTERM. Diff scope is limited to orchestrator/gate.py and tests/test_gate_timeout.py as specified. Gate metadata shows first_green_at already recorded externally with gate_reds: 0. One low-severity gap noted: the new test doesn't cover the SIGKILL-after-grace-timeout site (gate.py:69) for PermissionError, only the probe and the post-probe SIGKILL site \u2014 same fix pattern, just untested at that one spot. Not blocking.",
    "verdict": "approve",
    "comments": [
      {
        "path": "tests/test_gate_timeout.py",
        "line": 197,
        "issue": "test_killpg_permission_error_is_treated_as_gone exercises the probe (signal 0) and the post-probe SIGKILL (gate.py:83), but never drives the earlier SIGKILL-after-grace-timeout path (gate.py:69, hit when SIGTERM alone doesn't reap the process within kill_grace_s). That site got the same except-clause change but has no PermissionError-injection coverage.",
        "severity": "low"
      }
    ],
