    {
      "ts": 1790809788.548364,
      "status": "done",
      "result": {
        "summary": "Implementation matches spec: all four os.killpg call sites in gate._run now catch (ProcessLookupError, PermissionError) instead of ProcessLookupError alone, and the wall-clock deadline loop from T-1407 is preserved with correct return shape. Verified by reading orchestrator/gate.py and tests/test_gate_timeout.py at the T-1407 worktree HEAD (commit 98dfec7), and by running `uv run --project . python -m unittest discover -q tests -p test_gate_timeout.py` three times in a row: 14/14 tests pass each run, including test_killpg_permission_error_is_treated_as_gone and test_deadline_counts_wall_clock_sleep. Traced both subTest iterations (denied_signal=0 and denied_signal=SIGKILL) by hand against the implementation and confirmed each raises PermissionError at the intended callsite and is swallowed, with the process actually reaped via the real SIGTERM. Diff scope is limited to orchestrator/gate.py and tests/test_gate_timeout.py as specified. Gate metadata shows first_green_at already recorded externally with gate_reds: 0. One low-severity gap noted: the new test doesn't cover the SIGKILL-after-grace-timeout site (gate.py:69) for PermissionError, only the probe and the post-probe SIGKILL site \u2014 same fix pattern, just untested at that one spot. Not blocking.",
        "verdict": "approve",
        "comments": [
          {
            "path": "tests/test_gate_timeout.py",
            "line": 197,
            "issue": "test_killpg_permission_error_is_treated_as_gone exercises the probe (signal 0) and the post-probe SIGKILL (gate.py:83), but never drives the earlier SIGKILL-after-grace-timeout path (gate.py:69, hit when SIGTERM alone doesn't reap the process within kill_grace_s). That site got the same except-clause change but has no PermissionError-injection coverage.",
            "severity": "low"
          }
        ],
        "packet_version": "86dca6705ea4",
        "confidence": 0.0,
        "provenance": [
          "repo"
        ]
      }
